# You design and build LEGO Technic models one step at a time, in a build language.
# 
# For each step you write:
# ADD name partnumber color
# CONNECT part.point -> part.point LOCKED|TURNS|STIFF   (points: hole1.., axlehole1.., pin1.., axle1.., clip1..; LOCKED = cross in cross, turn together; TURNS = free; STIFF = friction pin)
# Optional: MESH a.teeth b.teeth / RATIO a b x/y / GROUP g (opens a side build) / END (closes it) / ATTACH g (joins a finished side build into the main model)
# WHY one plain sentence: what this step builds and what it is for.
# A point ending in ~ is an estimate; ? means not known.
# 
# Rules: only use real points of each part; a round pin never goes in a cross hole; a shaft that must turn needs round holes; a worm needs stops on both sides; gears must sit at the right distance.
STEP 1
ADD rear-crossaxle-1 44294 yellow
ADD rear-crossconnector-1 42003 darkturquoise
CONNECT rear-crossaxle-1.axle4 -> rear-crossconnector-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Centers a turquoise perpendicular connector on the seven-length rear cross axle.
STEP 2
ADD rear-halfpin-1 4274 lightgray
ADD rear-halfpin-2 4274 lightgray
CONNECT rear-halfpin-1.pin1 -> rear-crossconnector-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT rear-halfpin-2.pin1 -> rear-crossconnector-1.hole2 TURNS
WHY Adds two half pins in the rear connector with their stud ends exposed above the fuselage core.
STEP 3
ADD rear-side-link-1 32449 lightgray
ADD rear-tie-axle-1 32062 red
CONNECT rear-tie-axle-1.axle1 -> rear-side-link-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT rear-crossaxle-1.axle3~ -> rear-side-link-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Adds the first thin side link with a short red axle at its rear end.
STEP 4
ADD rear-side-link-2 32449 lightgray
ADD tail-root-beam-1 32140 white
CONNECT rear-tie-axle-1.axle1~ -> tail-root-beam-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT rear-tie-axle-1.axle2 -> rear-side-link-2.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT rear-crossaxle-1.axle5~ -> rear-side-link-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
WHY Traps the white tail-root beam between matching thin links on the red axle.
STEP 5
GROUP fuselage-left-base
ADD fuselage-lower-link-1 32449 lightgray
ADD fuselage-lower-beam-1 32065 white
ADD fuselage-lower-pin-1 61332 black
ADD fuselage-lower-pin-2 61332 black
ADD rear-cross-spacer-1 18654 white
CONNECT fuselage-lower-pin-1.pin1 -> fuselage-lower-link-1.hole1 STIFF
CONNECT fuselage-lower-pin-2.pin1 -> fuselage-lower-link-1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT fuselage-lower-pin-1.pin2 -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole6~ STIFF
CONNECT fuselage-lower-pin-2.pin2 -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole7~ STIFF
END
ATTACH fuselage-left-base
CONNECT rear-crossaxle-1.axle2~ -> rear-cross-spacer-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT rear-crossaxle-1.axle1~ -> fuselage-lower-link-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
WHY Builds the first long lower fuselage side and slides it onto the cross axle outside a white spacer.
STEP 6
ADD front-crossaxle-1 44294 yellow
ADD front-crossconnector-1 42003 darkturquoise
ADD front-crossconnector-2 42003 darkturquoise
ADD front-crossconnector-3 42003 darkturquoise
CONNECT front-crossaxle-1.axle4 -> front-crossconnector-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT front-crossaxle-1.axle3 -> front-crossconnector-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT front-crossaxle-1.axle5 -> front-crossconnector-3.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT front-crossaxle-1.axle1~ -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole4~ TURNS
WHY Groups three turquoise connectors on the front cross axle and fits them across the forward fuselage.
STEP 7
GROUP nose-drive
ADD nose-base-1 39793 white
ADD nose-shortpin-1 32002 tan
ADD nose-shortpin-2 32002 tan
CONNECT nose-shortpin-1.pin1 -> nose-base-1.hole1~ STIFF
CONNECT nose-shortpin-2.pin1 -> nose-base-1.hole8~ STIFF
WHY Places two short tan pins in the white nose base for mounting the bevel-drive assembly.
STEP 8
ADD nose-axlepin-1 18651 black
ADD nose-axlepin-2 18651 black
CONNECT nose-axlepin-1.pin1 -> nose-base-1.hole2~ STIFF
CONNECT nose-axlepin-2.pin1 -> nose-base-1.hole9~ STIFF
WHY Adds the two long axle pins that will secure the nose assembly across the fuselage sides.
STEP 9
ADD nose-drive-bracket-1 65746 black
CONNECT nose-drive-bracket-1.pin1? -> nose-base-1.hole4~ STIFF
CONNECT nose-drive-bracket-1.pin2? -> nose-base-1.hole6~ STIFF
WHY Seats the black drive bracket on the nose base with its two round shaft bearings upright.
STEP 10
ADD drive-vertical-axle-1 3705 black
ADD drive-bevel-gear-1 6589 tan
CONNECT drive-vertical-axle-1.axle1 -> drive-bevel-gear-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT drive-vertical-axle-1.axle2~ -> nose-drive-bracket-1.hole1? TURNS
CONNECT drive-vertical-axle-1.axle3~ -> nose-base-1.hole5 TURNS
WHY Drops the first bevel gear on its vertical axle through the bracket and nose base.
STEP 11
ADD propeller-axle-1 15462 brown
ADD drive-bevel-gear-2 6589 tan
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle2~ -> drive-bevel-gear-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle3~ -> nose-drive-bracket-1.hole2? TURNS
MESH drive-bevel-gear-1.teeth drive-bevel-gear-2.teeth
RATIO drive-bevel-gear-1 drive-bevel-gear-2 1/1
WHY Adds the stopped propeller shaft with a matching bevel gear to turn the drive through ninety degrees.
STEP 12
ADD nose-front-link-1 6632 white
ADD nose-front-link-2 6632 white
ADD nose-frame-axle-1 3705 black
ADD nose-frame-axle-2 3705 black
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-1.axle1~ -> nose-front-link-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-2.axle1~ -> nose-front-link-1.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-1.axle1~ -> nose-front-link-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-2.axle1~ -> nose-front-link-2.axlehole2 LOCKED
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle4~ -> nose-front-link-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle4~ -> nose-front-link-2.hole1 TURNS
WHY Braces the propeller shaft with paired white links while their round center holes let it rotate.
STEP 13
ADD nose-frame-spacer-1 18654 white
ADD nose-frame-spacer-2 18654 white
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-1.axle2~ -> nose-frame-spacer-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-2.axle2~ -> nose-frame-spacer-2.hole1 TURNS
WHY Slides white spacers onto both frame axles to keep the front nose pieces evenly separated.
STEP 14
ADD nose-front-crossaxle-1 3705 black
ADD nose-connector-1 42003 darkturquoise
ADD nose-connector-2 42003 darkturquoise
ADD nose-connector-3 42003 darkturquoise
CONNECT nose-front-crossaxle-1.axle1~ -> nose-connector-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-front-crossaxle-1.axle2~ -> nose-connector-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-front-crossaxle-1.axle3~ -> nose-connector-3.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-1.axle3~ -> nose-connector-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-2.axle3~ -> nose-connector-3.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle5 -> nose-connector-2.hole1 TURNS
WHY Closes the turquoise nose face around the propeller shaft and the two frame axles.
STEP 15
ADD nose-tooth-1 48267 orange
ADD nose-tooth-2 48267 orange
ADD propeller-pin-1 32054 orange
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-1.axle4 -> nose-tooth-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT nose-frame-axle-2.axle4 -> nose-tooth-2.axlehole1 LOCKED
CONNECT propeller-axle-1.axle5~ -> propeller-pin-1.axlehole1 LOCKED
END
WHY Fits the two orange nose teeth and locks the orange propeller pin onto the driven shaft.
STEP 16
ATTACH nose-drive
CONNECT nose-front-crossaxle-1.axle1~ -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole1 TURNS
CONNECT nose-shortpin-1.pin2 -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole2 STIFF
CONNECT nose-axlepin-1.axle1~ -> fuselage-lower-beam-1.hole4~ TURNS
WHY Attaches the complete bevel-drive nose to the first fuselage side at the three shown mounting points.
STEP 17
GROUP fuselage-right-base
